IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb1-part2-incorporation`

-- Tests of cb1-part2-incorporation.l4 (s 5 to s 14). Expected values are written from the text of the Act
-- (src:139-212), never from the code's output: each comment says what the text gives.

§ `Tests -- Part II incorporation`

§§ `s 5 incorporators`

-- src:140: one or more individuals or bodies corporate may incorporate by signing and complying with s 7.
#ASSERT `the signers may incorporate a corporation within s 5(1)` 1 0 TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `the signers may incorporate a corporation within s 5(1)` 0 1 TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `the signers may incorporate a corporation within s 5(1)` 2 3 TRUE TRUE
-- nobody signs: not "one or more"
#ASSERT NOT (`the signers may incorporate a corporation within s 5(1)` 0 0 TRUE TRUE)
-- an individual who may not incorporate signs
#ASSERT NOT (`the signers may incorporate a corporation within s 5(1)` 1 0 FALSE TRUE)
-- section 7 not complied with
#ASSERT NOT (`the signers may incorporate a corporation within s 5(1)` 1 0 TRUE FALSE)

-- src:143-145: not less than 18; not incapable; not bankrupt. Boundary on the age: 17 fails, 18 passes.
#ASSERT `the individual may incorporate a corporation within s 5(2)` 18 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `the individual may incorporate a corporation within s 5(2)` 65 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the individual may incorporate a corporation within s 5(2)` 17 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- incapable under a province's law (not by minority)
#ASSERT NOT (`the individual may incorporate a corporation within s 5(2)` 30 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- an inability that is by reason of minority does not make the person incapable under s 2(1)
#ASSERT `the individual may incorporate a corporation within s 5(2)` 30 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- declared incapable by a court outside Canada
#ASSERT NOT (`the individual may incorporate a corporation within s 5(2)` 30 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- bankrupt
#ASSERT NOT (`the individual may incorporate a corporation within s 5(2)` 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)

§§ `s 6 articles of incorporation`

-- a plain one-class corporation with a fixed number of directors and no restrictions (src:147-155)
`articles plain` MEANS `Articles of incorporation as delivered (s 6(1))` WITH
    `follow the form that the Director fixes` IS TRUE
    `set out the name of the corporation` IS TRUE
    `set out the province in Canada where the registered office is to be situated` IS TRUE
    `set out the classes and any maximum number of shares that the corporation is authorized to issue` IS TRUE
    `there will be two or more classes of shares` IS FALSE
    `set out the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to each class of shares` IS FALSE
    `a class of shares may be issued in series` IS FALSE
    `set out the authority given to the directors to fix the number of shares in, and to determine the designation of, and the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to, the shares of each series` IS FALSE
    `the issue, transfer or ownership of shares of the corporation is to be restricted` IS FALSE
    `set out a statement to that effect and a statement as to the nature of the restrictions` IS FALSE
    `set out the number of directors` IS TRUE
    `set out the minimum and maximum number of directors` IS FALSE
    `paragraph 107(a) allows a minimum and maximum number of directors` IS FALSE
    `there are restrictions on the businesses that the corporation may carry on` IS FALSE
    `set out the restrictions on the businesses that the corporation may carry on` IS FALSE

